-- title:
--   Additivity in a of the cyclic carry class in H²
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group generated by a single element $s$, in the sense that every $g\in G$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $s$, and assume $s$ has finite order $n=\operatorname{orderOf} s$. For $g\in G$ let $\mathrm{cyclicLog}(g)\in\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ be the exponent attached to $g$ by the canonical bijection between $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ and the powers of $s$, and for a representation $A$ of $G$ over $\mathbb Z$ and an element $a$ of $A$ let $\mathrm{carryFun}(a):G\times G\to A$ be the $2$-cochain sending $(g,h)$ to $a$ when $\mathrm{cyclicLog}(g)+\mathrm{cyclicLog}(h)\ge n$, i.e. when the addition of exponents carries, and to $0$ otherwise. Given $a,b$ in $A$, and assuming that each of the three cochains $\mathrm{carryFun}(a)$, $\mathrm{carryFun}(b)$ and $\mathrm{carryFun}(a+b)$ lies in the module `cocycles₂ A` of inhomogeneous $2$-cocycles, the theorem asserts that under the quotient map `H2π A` from $2$-cocycles to $H^2(G,A)$ the class of $\mathrm{carryFun}(a+b)$ equals the sum of the classes of $\mathrm{carryFun}(a)$ and $\mathrm{carryFun}(b)$. The cocycle condition on $\mathrm{carryFun}(a+b)$ is taken as a hypothesis rather than deduced from the other two.
--
--   The carry cochain is the standard explicit $2$-cocycle on a finite cyclic group obtained from the carries in the addition of exponents; this statement records that its cohomology class depends additively on the coefficient $a$. It is used in the construction of the local fundamental class, via [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.isLocalFundamentalClass_of_pin`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.isLocalFundamentalClass_of_pin).
